# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — AGENTS.md

## Purpose

This file is the single source of truth for AI collaboration rules in this repository. It carries only the minimal high-level rules every AI must always know, plus operating invariants, the Definition of Done, and coarse routing pointers. Details route into `aiDoc/`.

## Loading Model

- **L0 auto-loaded**: the root `CLAUDE.md` imports this file via `@AGENTS.md` in every session. This file never expands details and never lists the full document inventory.
- **L1 task routing**: `aiDoc/README.md` is the sole maintained home of the doc index and the "task → must-read docs" routing table. On receiving a task, consult that routing table first to decide which child docs to read.
- **L2 on-demand deep read**: the concrete `aiDoc/` child documents the routing table points to.
- **Conflict priority** (for in-repo tasks): `AGENTS.md` > `aiDoc/README.md` > aiDoc child docs > tool adapter files.

## Tool Loading

| Tool | Loading mechanism |
|---|---|
| Claude Code | Root `CLAUDE.md` natively imports `@AGENTS.md`; `.claude/commands/` holds project commands only — no rule adapter files |
| Trae | `.trae/rules/project_rules.md` thin adapter points to `AGENTS.md` |
| Cursor / Copilot / other | If `@import` is unsupported, create a thin adapter at the tool's native rules path: entry pointers only, never copied rule bodies |

No tool-private directory may hold a copy of project-level rules. This table is the only index of tool adaptation state — register every adapter here.

