### Doc Maintenance

High-level rules live in this file; details live in `aiDoc/`. This file keeps only coarse "task family → aiDoc area" pointers (see Task Routing below). The detailed file-level routing table is maintained solely in `aiDoc/README.md` — never duplicate the full inventory here, or the two copies will drift.

### Code-Reading Constraints

Never read generated, vendored, or cached trees: `node_modules/`, `.venv/`, `__pycache__/`, `vendor/`, `dist/`, `build/`, lock files, and similar. Read source and manifests instead.

## Operating Invariants

- One fact has one maintained home; everywhere else links to it.
- Rule bodies live only in `AGENTS.md` and `aiDoc/`; tool-private directories hold pointers only.
- Non-trivial decisions are recorded in `aiDoc/notes/`; multi-step changes are planned in `aiDoc/plans/`.
- Evidence is proportional to the affected surface: run focused checks for the surface you touched, not the full suite by reflex. Never weaken filters or thresholds to get green.
- A push, merge, deployment, or interrupted process is not successful until its observable acceptance check passes.

## Definition of Done

- Code follows the layering and module rules documented in `aiDoc/`.
- Both sides of every changed contract (producer and consumer) are traced and updated; `aiDoc/contracts/boundary.md` is updated when applicable.
- Required evidence ran and passed; passed / failed / skipped / not-run are reported separately.
- Decision notes and memory indexes are updated when the change alters behavior, contracts, process, testing strategy, or persistent data.
- When work is handed off unfinished, the handoff records exact state, changed files, commands run with results, remaining work, blockers, and the next safe action. An interrupted command is never described as completed.

